      "text": "So thank you. And let's talk. Well, we believe that technology is not neutral. It carries world bills, politicals and economic choices and above all, real impacts people's lives. So that's why we argue that the voice of those most affected by digital transformation must be at the center of this conversation. In other words, and discussion about technological innovations should begin with the need, right, and leave it experience of the people who are directly impacted. And very often is not the case when we look at how regulations are made and how the process of governance are conducive. Over the past 10 years, we have structured our work at Iris, the Institute for Research on Internet and Society in three main lines.",
