      "end": 226.71,
      "duration": 88.17,
      "text": "And the first is security and technology, where we cause the importance of digital tools for privacy, data protections, the right to encryption, and how to face gender violence online. Other things. The second is meaningful connectivity, which focuses not only on physical access to the Internet, but also on the conditions to enable full critical and transformative participation in the digital environment. And finally, we have social governance of technology, which address social innovation, governance, participation, and the creation of a sustainable and inclusive technological future. Brazil is historically an equal country, and it's our responsibility to understand how systems of discrimination and exclusion have evolved over time, so we can effectively address that. One basic challenge nowadays is the level of digital literacy of our population that still needs to improve significantly to ensure that everyone can benefit from new technologies.",
