      "fragment_index": 5,
      "start": 323.46,
      "end": 414.34,
      "duration": 90.88,
      "text": "In the recent years, part of our work has focused on artificial intelligence in Brazil, and we have contributed to building a solidary regulatory framework and strengthening social narratives capable of guiding the development of technology in a close, inclusive and anti-discriminatory way. This is crucial, giving the increasingly clear evidence that historically marginalized groups, including black people, indigenous people, transgender individuals, people with disabilities, have been disproportionately harmed by the rapid and often uncritical development of AI systems. Recognizing this problem is the first step, and the second is to build collectively and democratically mechanisms to ensure technology serves to fight against discrimination and promote social justice. As a research institution, one of a very often challenge is having the support needed to develop a genuinely Brazilian understanding of AI dilemmas and possibilities, and to often we find ourselves debating regulations important from the global north, which may be relevant in the own context,",
