      "text": "Its press has been long and involving hundreds of written contributions, numerals, public hearings, an international seminar, the creation of a commission of jurists, and a Senate Comchi dedicated to the topic. That makes it the most advanced AI legislative proposal currently in Brazil. And the draft incorporates key elements for education and responsible AI development, including risk-based approach, the creation of a list of rights, proportional governance measures, an institutional oversight framework, and mechanisms to incentivize responsible innovation. Some highlights that I could share with you are symmetric regulation based on risk levels, preventing regulatory overload for low-risk systems, establishing of basic rights and guarantees for individuals potentially affected.",
