      "end": 722.84,
      "duration": 77.35,
      "text": "And we believe that AI is undoubtedly a technology of our time, but as the title of this panel suggests we cannot find blind, and its costs are not fully clear and neither are its benefits. It is therefore essential to ensure that benefits are fairly distributed, and that costs do not fall in the most vulnerable populations. In Brazil, conflicts are already emerging within communities and companies thinking to establish data centers, with debates about energy, socio-economic, and for environment impact, and at the same time, considering inequalities in internet access, meaningful connectivity, and low-digital literacy, it becomes evident that the benefits of the digital technologies are not equitably distributed. In many cases, they are far from addressing the most urgent needs of our population.",
